WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.020
SCP-682 Vs SCP-743.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.879
Could the world’s most terrifying chocolate
fountain, filled with an endless supply of

00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:11.960
omnivorous insects, finally be the thing to
fell the Hard to Destroy Reptile?

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.990
Initially, there seemed to be hope.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:19.030
Exactly as the Foundation intended, 682 consumed
some of the delicious chocolate, marking it

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.000
for death by the nightmarish creatures lurking
within.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.300
The swarm soon burst from the fountain and
began attacking and devouring SCP-682.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.750
The creatures consumed 21% of 682’s mass
before the monster finally fought back.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:37.789
It evolved a long, anteater-like tongue that
it used to catch and eat many of the insects.

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:41.239
The insects and 682 fed off each other for
days.

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:46.090
And after the two were separated, having consumed
743’s chocolate appeared to have temporarily

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.550
given 682 heightened regenerative abilities.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.670
After observing this, the researchers concluded
that the two anomalies should never be brought

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.329
into contact again.

